# Fast jets now hold for a large-safe landing runway instead of using an otherwise
# available short strip. T5j2 deliberately contains mixed-runway airports under
# contention, so removing that unsafe extra jet capacity lowers its deterministic
# five-year total from the previous baseline while preserving forward progress.
#
# Re-baselined for the upstream 16.x merge (782 upstream commits). All three fixtures
# moved, in both directions -- mass7-inair 9153 -> 9251, helis2 13437 -> 13816, T5j2
# 6332 -> 6309 -- which reads as upstream changing aircraft and economy behaviour
# rather than a routing regression: a broken reservation or pathfinding path depresses
# throughput on every fixture, and two of three rose.
#
# The floor has more headroom than the other two fixtures on purpose. Migrating this
# save to version 375 shifted it by 26 movements (6283 before the re-save, 6309 after),
# while mass7-inair and helis2 both round-tripped to the exact same totals. Whatever
# state does not survive T5j2's save/load is worth about half a percent here, so a
# 30-movement margin of the kind the other fixtures use would be inside the noise.
min_movements=6250
